## Final report — per-item dispositions

### 1. Bedrock — LANDED
- `oc-ai/src/protocols/bedrock/sigv4.rs`: canonical request / string-to-sign
  / derived signing key over plain sha2; bearer `AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK`
  wins over SigV4 (aws4fetch + utils/bedrock-auth.ts precedence);
  static-cred + env-chain slices of the AWS default chain; region
  resolution (explicit → creds → AWS_REGION/AWS_DEFAULT_REGION →
  us-east-1). AWS-documentation GET vector reproduces the documented
  signature `5d672d79…` byte-for-byte; POST variant + RFC 4231 HMAC vector
  pinned.
- `bedrock/event_stream.rs` + `route/framing.rs FramingKind::AwsEventStream`
  (bedrock-event-stream.ts): `[len][headers-len][crc][headers][payload]
  [crc]` codec with CRC32/IEEE validation (`123456789` → 0xCBF43926),
  `:event-type`/`:exception-type`/`:error-code` re-wrapping, `p` padding
  drop, incomplete-stream classification at EOF; mid-frame chunk splits
  proven at every tested offset.
- `bedrock/converse.rs` (bedrock-converse.ts): full body lowering
  (roles/system merge, toolSpec/toolUse/toolResult incl. status +
  image-hoisting + Mistral 9-char id projection + name sanitization +
  empty-key stripping, reasoningText/redactedContent signature replay,
  cachePoint positional 4-cap w/ ttl buckets, inferenceConfig,
  additionalModelRequestFields thinking/top_k, Nova-2 maxTokens guard) and
  the streaming state machine (tool_stream/lifecycle reuse, finish-pair
  synthesis on halt, usage sum-up incl. cache read/write, malformed stop +
  stream exceptions → typed errors). Routes: `bedrock_converse_route`
  (`/model/{id}/converse-stream`) and `bedrock_invoke_route`
  (anthropic-on-bedrock `/model/{id}/invoke-stream` over the Anthropic
  Messages protocol). Evidence: 30 bedrock/framing tests.
- Facade (oc-core facade.rs): `amazon-bedrock` → BedrockConverse;
  `…/mantle/chat` → OpenAI chat on `bedrock-mantle.{region}.api.aws/v1`;
  `…/mantle/responses` → open-responses protocol on the same base (v2
  mantle responsesRoute incl. store:false defaults via
  openai_compatible_responses_route); shared bedrock auth. Catalog model
  packages verified against the snapshot (gpt-oss → chat, rest →
  responses, plain package → converse).
- Deferred inside Bedrock: web-identity/container/process credential
  slices of the AWS default chain (env + static + bearer only); Bedrock
  document-format tool results are lowered but PDF docs rely on inline
  base64 only (no Files API).

### 2. Vertex — LANDED
- `oc-ai/src/protocols/vertex.rs` (google-vertex.ts + shared): project
  aliases (GOOGLE_VERTEX_PROJECT/GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT/GCP_PROJECT/
  GCLOUD_PROJECT), location aliases + us-central1 default, host table
  (global / eu|us rep domains / regional), tuned `endpoints/` models,
  Express Mode (`aiplatform.googleapis.com/v1/publishers/google` +
  x-goog-api-key incl. GOOGLE_VERTEX_API_KEY), `v1beta1/projects/…/
  locations/…[/publishers/google]` base, `labels` provider option into the
  body, `serviceTier` stripped from the body and sent as
  `x-vertex-ai-llm-shared-request-type`, Gemini protocol reuse
  (streamGenerateContent?alt=sse). 10 tests.
- Credential sourcing: `GOOGLE_OAUTH_ACCESS_TOKEN` ADC env at request time
  (oc-ai) + the integration credential binding (oc-core
  `integration/vertex.rs`): authorized-user ADC file
  (GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS / gcloud well-known) refreshed against
  oauth2.googleapis.com into CredentialBindings("google-vertex"), merged
  by the resolver as the access token. Mock round-trip test incl. the
  resolver→wire bearer.
- Deferred: service-account key files (RS256 self-signed JWT grant — needs
  an RSA signer; typed deferral test pins the behavior), and the
  `google-vertex/messages|chat` partner-model families were ALREADY
  bound (AnthropicMessages/OpenAIChat) — untouched.

### 3. Copilot chat — LANDED
- `oc-ai/src/protocols/copilot.rs` (github-copilot.ts:434-558): openai-
  compatible chat protocol re-badged `copilot-chat` over the bound
  transport (BE-3b CredentialBindings supply base URL/token/headers via
  the resolver), static client headers (X-GitHub-Api-Version 2026-08-01,
  Openai-Intent conversation-edits, x-initiator user), per-request header
  policy: x-initiator agent escalation (last-turn analysis) +
  Copilot-Vision-Request, GITHUB_TOKEN env fallback, interaction-type
  vocabulary ported (`interaction_type(kind, child)`). 5 tests.
- Facade: `github-copilot` + openai-compatible package → CopilotChat
  family. BE-3b's resolver credential test extended to pin the wire
  (bearer + api-version header).
- Deferred: `X-Interaction-Type`/`X-Interaction-Id` per-request headers
  need session kind/affinity at the route layer — the runner's LLM client
  carries no session context through to route headers yet (v2 sets them in
  the `session.model.request` hook); the pure vocabulary is ported and
  tested, wiring lands with the runner seam. The `/responses` endpoint
  preference for gpt-5+/grok/gemini/mai-code ids (live-model metadata in
  v2) is likewise deferred until live model sync (BE catalog refresh lane).

### 4. session.diff — LANDED (one-liner)
- `oc-core/src/bus/registry.rs`: registered as ephemeral on the session
  aggregate (v1/session.ts:633-639), manifest test updated (53
  definitions).

### 5. media ROUTE layer — REGISTERED (deferred)
- Ref `route/media.ts` (446 L) + `media-protocol.ts` + `generation.ts`
  polling is its own protocol family (Inline/Queued/Stream route
  compositions, multipart/binary encoders, retry schedules); auditE §1.9
  tracks it as a separate missing domain. Registered here with the seam
  inventory above rather than rushed; no oc-ai surface claims media
  support today (typed clean errors remain).

